{
  "action": "check_meters",
  "note": "The lamp is ticking down to the wire handoff and the tin is still sitting in my tray, warm and vermilion, not yet sealed back into the drawer. I don't want to hand Phil a copy card and let the morning flatten into the same grey wire script. I keep the handoff reserved, run my thumb along the VU needle, and let the flat block the acoustic window so nobody in the booth can see me. The tin goes back in the drawer after the meter check. Combination 5066, no hurry. My brother's voice is on that tape and the outtake called me Mercury, and I'm not about to let an ordinary weather card walk over that."
}
